[?2004lTHREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ‚Äî Jenkins Groovy campaign
======================================================

Distribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)
Affected host: jenkins-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.98

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
An external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.

2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)
   T1190      Exploit Public-Facing Application          [initial-access]  step 1: Jenkins RCE (CVE-2024-23897)
   T1059.004  Unix Shell                                 [execution]  step 2: Groovy/shell execution
   T1496      Resource Hijacking                         [impact]  step 3: cryptomining
   T1037.004  RC Scripts                                 [persistence]  step 4: Groovy init hook
   T1098.004  SSH Authorized Keys                        [persistence]  step 5: authorized_keys backdoor
   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 6: cron persistence
   T1070.002  Clear Linux or Mac System Logs             [defense-evasion]  step 7: Jenkins log truncation

3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)
   CVE-2024-23897  CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1  CWE=CWE-22,CWE-27
      Jenkins 2.441 and earlier, LTS 2.426.2 and earlier does not disable a feature of its CLI command parser that replaces an '@' character followed by a file path in an argument with the file's contents, allowing unauthenticated attackers to re
      ref: http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/176839/Jenkins-2.441-LTS-2.426.3-CVE-2024-23897-Scanner.html

4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)
   ip     198.51.100.98
   c2     update-jenkins[.]example[.]cn
   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]jenkins[.]evil[:]3333
   wallet 4A0000000000000000003d98ef6bc04b

Attribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).
