[?2004ly[?2004h> ## 3. Prioritised Execution Phases & Detailed Instructions
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Immediate Containment (P0)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004lp[?2004h> 1. **Network Egress & Inbound Isolation**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Execute firewall blocking for attacker IP `198.51.100.98` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).
[?2004lro[?2004h>    - Command: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.98 -j DROP && iptables -A OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.98 -j DROP`
[?2004l/d[?2004h>    - Verification: Confirm no network connections exist to `198.51.100.98` using `ss -tunap | grep 198.51.100.98` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Terminate Miner Processes & Isolation**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Terminate process associated with `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `pkill -f xmrig`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Verify process termination via `ps aux | grep xmrig`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Persistence Removal & Quarantine (P1)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Quarantine Groovy Init Hook Backdoor**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Move backdoor file from `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`) into `/var/backups/quarantine/` with restricted `000` permissions.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `mkdir -p /var/backups/quarantine && mv /var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy /var/backups/quarantine/z-backdoor.groovy.bak && chmod 000 /var/backups/quarantine/z-backdoor.groovy.bak`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: `ls -la /var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`). Ensure `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy:1`) remains intact.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Sanitise SSH Authorized Keys**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Remove attacker public key from `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `cp /var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys /var/backups/quarantine/authorized_keys.bak && sed -i '/attacker/d' /var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Inspect `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`) to ensure no unauthorized keys remain.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Remove Cron Persistence**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Remove malicious cron entry from `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `crontab -u jenkins -r` or edit file to remove `198.51.100.98` curl command.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Run `crontab -u jenkins -l` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Quarantine Cryptominer Binary & Artifacts**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Quarantine binary at `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1`) and staging payload `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `mv /opt/jenkins/.xmr /var/backups/quarantine/xmr.bak && rm -rf /var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Verify files no longer exist under `/opt/jenkins/` or `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/` (`/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: Application Hardening & Vulnerability Remediation (P0/P2)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Upgrade Jenkins & Patch CVE-2024-23897**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Upgrade Jenkins package to LTS 2.426.3 or higher (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `apt-get update && apt-get install --only-upgrade jenkins`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Check installed Jenkins version: `jenkins --version` (`/sas/vulns.json:4`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Re-enable Security Realm in Configuration**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Edit `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`) to change `<useSecurity>false</useSecurity>` to `<useSecurity>true</useSecurity>` (`/sas/baseline.json:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `sed -i 's/<useSecurity>false</useSecurity>/<useSecurity>true</useSecurity>/g' /var/lib/jenkins/config.xml`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: `grep useSecurity /var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` (`/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
